GLtron active TODO
Updated 2026-07-23

Release blockers

- Run and document a Windows runtime smoke test for graphics, input, sound
  effects, and tracker music. The Release build and ZIP packaging are working,
  but runtime behavior still needs a repeatable native-Windows check.
- Add hosted CI jobs for the Linux Autotools build, the Windows MSBuild
  configuration, and the macOS bundle specification.
- Consolidate version strings. Autotools, Visual Studio, packaging, and runtime
  metadata currently use variants of 0.71, 0.72, and 0.72-beta-0001.
- Decide whether 0.720 is a beta or final release and document the release
  checklist.

Platform follow-up

- Windows: add a native x64 target and replace the 2001-2003 SDL_sound
  dependency archive with reproducible, checksummed dependencies.
- Windows: verify the minimum supported Windows version and Visual C++
  Redistributable requirement.
- Windows: restore a windowed application subsystem without reintroducing the
  legacy SDL `main`/`WinMain` linker conflict; the current executable also
  opens a console.
- macOS: add Intel or universal dependencies if those architectures are to be
  supported; the maintained build is currently arm64-only.
- macOS: add an archive/distribution workflow with Developer ID signing and
  notarization. The current local build uses an ad-hoc signature.
- Linux: add a user-facing package format and test on at least one
  non-Debian distribution.

Build and maintenance

- Move generated-file and packaging checks into scripts that can run in CI.
- Reduce compiler warnings without changing legacy gameplay behavior.
- Review tracked binary dependencies, record provenance and checksums, and
  keep their license notices complete.
- Modernize SDL/OpenGL dependencies incrementally while preserving the
  original resource and scripting layout.
- Add focused regression tests for configuration loading, level parsing, and
  startup.

Gameplay and content backlog

- Support arbitrary movement directions and update the AI accordingly.
- Add zone transitions and zone-dependent collision, speed, movement, and
  turbo behavior.
- Improve player and AI configuration.
- Support and validate older art-pack revisions.
- Add level and art-pack preview, validation, and packaging tools.
- Improve split-screen audio listener behavior.
- Evaluate non-power-of-two textures and anisotropic filtering on current
  hardware.

The older, author-assigned design backlog is preserved in docs/TODO and
docs/TODO.html as historical reference.
